<title>NETHERLANDS: HISTORIC GUILDER/MARK EXCHANGE RATES.</title>
<headline>HISTORIC GUILDER/MARK EXCHANGE RATES.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank raised</p>
<p>interest rates on Monday in an attempt to counter recent</p>
<p>weakness of the guilder against the German mark.</p>
<p>Historic average monthly and yearly guilder/mark exchange</p>
<p>rates are listed below in guilders per 100 marks (source Central</p>
<p>Bureau of Statistics/Nederlandsche Bank):</p>
<p>    Spot 11/3/97	Feb 97  Jan 97</p>
<p>    112.55/56	   112.33  112.30</p>
<p>    Dec 96   Nov 96   Oct 96   Sep 96   Aug 96   Jul 96</p>
<p>    112.21   112.16   112.18   112.11   112.17   112.23</p>
<p>    Jun 96   May 96   Apr 96   Mar 96   Feb 96   Jan 96</p>
<p>    112.02   111.81   111.82   111.93   111.98   111.99</p>
<p>    Yr  96   Yr  95   Yr  94   Yr  93   Yr  92   Yr  91</p>
<p>    112.05   112.02   112.15   112.34   112.60   112.69</p>
<p>    Yr  90   Yr  89   Yr  88   Yr  87   Yr  86   Yr  85</p>
<p>    112.67   112.81   112.55   112.69   112.82   112.80</p>
<p>    Yr  84   Yr  83   Yr  82   Yr  81   Yr  80   Yr  79</p>
<p>    112.75   111.75   110.03   110.35   109.36   109.48</p>
<p>NOTE -- The guilder's central rate against the mark in the</p>
<p>EU's exchange rate mechanism (ERM) is 112.673 per 100 marks.</p>
<p>It is allowed to fluctuate within a band of 2.25 percent</p>
<p>either side of that central rate.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsroom +31 20 504 5000, Fax +31 20 504 5040</p>
</text>
